Ported from a downstream Kilo fork (author: Daniel Sali), rebased onto the
upstream base pinned in the Dockerfile plus feat-add-cross-mesh-granularity.diff.
The fork's README changes are left out.

- Coalesce remote Node watch events over a 1s debounce window before
  rebuilding the topology.
- Replace per-rule iptables fork/exec loops with atomic iptables-restore /
  ip6tables-restore --noflush transactions, and skip KILO-NAT population when
  no POSTROUTING jump exists.
- Ignore remote discovered-endpoints updates that cannot affect local
  WireGuard peer endpoints (PersistentKeepalive == 0, same-location nodes in
  cross mode, or keys already shadowed by a local handshake).
- Keep a segment leader's existing valid WireGuard IP across topology rebuilds
  and agent restarts, so nodes joining or leaving no longer renumber existing
  peers (context: https://github.com/squat/kilo/issues/549).
- Keep the wireguard-ip annotation when the agent cleans up on shutdown, so
  a restarted agent reuses its address instead of allocating a fresh one
  from an incomplete view of the mesh and renumbering its neighbours on
  every rolling update.

